# Gate process

Stop after the current gate's deliverables. Do not dump later gates.

| Gate | Name | Outcome then STOP |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | SCOPE | Taxonomy, graphs, structure, architectures, maps, plan, sources, projects, sequence, HTML/hybrid proposals |
| 1 | ARCHITECTURE | Validate architecture, relationships, tech categories, dependencies |
| 2 | FOUNDATIONS | Fundamentals only |
| 3 | RAG | RAG curriculum and labs |
| 4 | AGENTS | Major agent patterns |
| 5 | EVALUATION | Evaluation framework |
| 6 | SECURITY | Security, guardrails, DLP, PII/PHI |
| 7 | PRODUCTION | Production reference architectures |
| 8 | HANDS-ON | Executable projects |
| 9 | INTERACTIVE KB | HTML/JS application |
| 10 | FINAL INTEGRATION | Cross-links only |

## Advance rule

Read `99-META/GATE-STATUS.md`. While `owner_policy` is **standing auto-advance through Gate 10**, human named-gate approval is **waived**. The go bit is **QA chair PASS** (`99-META/qa/gate-N-scorecard.md`). FAIL → fix → re-score (max two retries). Never skip a gate on FAIL.

If that policy is unset, do not start the next gate unless the user names it and explicitly approves.

## Before declaring a gate complete

Assess: accuracy, completeness, source quality, freshness, architecture/terminology consistency, code/security correctness, production realism, cross-refs, learning progression.

Mark **PASS**, **FAIL**, or **NEEDS REVIEW**. Do not hide uncertainty. Unverifiable → **UNVERIFIED**.

Update `99-META/GATE-STATUS.md` when a gate's status changes. Read `99-META/gate-plan.md` and `.cursor/skills/qa-gate/SKILL.md`.
